20:["$","p","That absence is a symptom, not a personality. Depression narrows the brain’s reward signalling, so activities that used to pay off no longer register — which makes withdrawal feel rational and deepens the loop.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"That absence is a symptom, not a personality. Depression narrows the brain’s reward signalling, so activities that used to pay off no longer register — which makes withdrawal feel rational and deepens the loop."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","In depression, the anticipation of reward dims before the capacity for it does. You can still enjoy a walk; you simply cannot feel in advance that you would. Waiting to feel like it means waiting for the last symptom to lift first.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"In depression, the anticipation of reward dims before the capacity for it does. You can still enjoy a walk; you simply cannot feel in advance that you would. Waiting to feel like it means waiting for the last symptom to lift first."}],["$","p","This is why behavioural activation works: small scheduled actions taken without motivation slowly restore the reward signal. Mood follows movement rather than leading it.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"This is why behavioural activation works: small scheduled actions taken without motivation slowly restore the reward signal. Mood follows movement rather than leading it."}]]]}]
